  user_input {
    user_response: "Build a complete native Android app named \"BossVsLeader\" using Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, and Material 3 (M3). Generate all files with full, compilable code. Do not use placeholders or \"TODO\" comments.\n\n## 1. APP CONCEPT\nBossVsLeader is a modern micro-learning app that teaches the difference between a Boss (commands, controls, blames) and a Leader (inspires, coaches, takes responsibility). Users read short lessons, take quizzes, compare Boss vs Leader behaviors, save favorites, and track their learning progress.\n\n## 2. TECH STACK\n- Language: Kotlin\n- UI: Jetpack Compose with Material 3 (androidx.compose.material3)\n- Architecture: MVVM + Repository pattern, with StateFlow and ViewModel\n- Navigation: Navigation Compose (single-activity)\n- Database: SQLite via SQLiteOpenHelper (no Room, no cloud). Use a DatabaseHelper class with explicit CREATE TABLE statements, CRUD functions, and a DAO-style wrapper. Run all DB calls on Dispatchers.IO via coroutines.\n- Min SDK 26, Target SDK 34\n- Provide build.gradle.kts (app and project), AndroidManifest.xml, and the full package structure\n\n## 3. SPLASH SCREEN (exactly 3 seconds)\n- Show for exactly 3000 ms, then navigate to Home. Remove the splash from the back stack.\n- Dark gradient background (deep navy to purple).\n- Centered animated logo: a crown icon (Leader) that scales in with a spring animation, plus a whistle/megaphone icon (Boss) that fades out and slides away. Draw both with Compose Canvas or Material icons.\n- App name \"BossVsLeader\" fades in letter by letter, with a tagline: \"Lead. Don\'t just boss.\"\n- A thin animated progress bar fills over the full 3 seconds.\n- Implement with LaunchedEffect(Unit) { delay(3000); navigate }.\n\n## 4. ANIMATED TOP NAVIGATION BAR (signature feature)\nBuild a custom animated top bar, not the default TopAppBar:\n- Collapsing behavior: expands to a large header with title and subtitle at the top of the list and shrinks smoothly on scroll (use nestedScroll with TopAppBarDefaults.exitUntilCollapsedScrollBehavior or a custom implementation).\n- Animated gradient background that slowly shifts colors (Boss red/orange to Leader blue/teal) using rememberInfiniteTransition.\n- Animated tab indicator: a pill that slides between tabs (Home, Lessons, Compare, Quiz, Profile) with animateDpAsState and a spring spec. The active tab icon scales and the label fades in.\n- Title cross-fades (AnimatedContent) when the destination changes.\n- Show the user\'s streak as a small flame badge with a pulse animation.\n- Handle edge-to-edge and status bar insets correctly.\n\n## 5. SCREENS\n1. Home: greeting, \"Lesson of the Day\" card, progress ring (Canvas), streak counter, quick-action chips.\n2. Lessons: LazyColumn of lesson cards grouped by category (Communication, Trust, Accountability, Motivation, Decision-Making, Feedback). Each has an icon, title, read time, and a completed checkmark. Tap to open the detail screen.\n3. Lesson Detail: a \"Boss\" panel (red) and a \"Leader\" panel (blue) side by side, with an example scenario, a key takeaway, a bookmark button, and a \"Mark as completed\" button with a confetti or check animation.\n4. Compare: swipeable cards (HorizontalPager) of \"Boss says / Leader says\" pairs, with a flip animation on tap.\n5. Quiz: multiple choice, a progress indicator, animated correct/incorrect feedback, and a final score screen with a retry option. Save the score to SQLite.\n6. Profile: stats (lessons completed, quizzes taken, average score, streak), a bookmarks list, a dark/light theme toggle, and a \"Reset progress\" button with a confirmation dialog.\n\n## 6. SQLITE SCHEMA\n- lessons(id INTEGER PK, title TEXT, category TEXT, boss_text TEXT, leader_text TEXT, scenario TEXT, takeaway TEXT, read_minutes INTEGER, is_completed INTEGER DEFAULT 0, is_bookmarked INTEGER DEFAULT 0)\n- quiz_questions(id INTEGER PK, question TEXT, option_a TEXT, option_b TEXT, option_c TEXT, option_d TEXT, correct_option INTEGER, explanation TEXT, category TEXT)\n- quiz_results(id INTEGER PK, score INTEGER, total INTEGER, taken_at INTEGER)\n- user_stats(id INTEGER PK, streak_days INTEGER, last_active_date TEXT, theme_mode TEXT)\nSeed the database on first launch (onCreate) with at least 20 lessons and 30 quiz questions of real, high-quality content about boss vs leader behavior. Provide the full seed data in code.\n\n## 7. DESIGN\n- Material 3 with a custom ColorScheme: Boss = warm red/orange, Leader = deep blue/teal, neutral surfaces.\n- Full light and dark themes, with dynamic color on Android 12+ as an option.\n- Modern look: rounded 24dp corners, soft elevation, glassmorphism-style cards, gradient accents, generous spacing, and a custom Typography scale.\n- Micro-interactions: animated list item entrance (staggered fade and slide-up), press-scale on cards, and smooth screen transitions (AnimatedNavHost with fade and slide).\n- Use Material Symbols icons (androidx.compose.material:material-icons-extended).\n\n## 8. QUALITY REQUIREMENTS\n- Handle configuration changes and process death (rememberSaveable and ViewModel).\n- Add content descriptions for accessibility and support large font sizes.\n- No crashes on empty states. Show friendly empty-state UIs.\n- Clean code with comments and meaningful names.\n- Output the complete project file tree first, then every file\'s full code in order, then short run instructions for Android Studio.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    items {
      item {
        text_block {
          content: "---\ntype: \"feature\"\ntitle: \"Build an Android app\"\nicon: \"android_color\"\n---\n\n"
        }
      }
    }
    items {
      text: "Build a complete native Android app named \"BossVsLeader\" using Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, and Material 3 (M3). Generate all files with full, compilable code. Do not use placeholders or \"TODO\" comments.\n\n## 1. APP CONCEPT\nBossVsLeader is a modern micro-learning app that teaches the difference between a Boss (commands, controls, blames) and a Leader (inspires, coaches, takes responsibility). Users read short lessons, take quizzes, compare Boss vs Leader behaviors, save favorites, and track their learning progress.\n\n## 2. TECH STACK\n- Language: Kotlin\n- UI: Jetpack Compose with Material 3 (androidx.compose.material3)\n- Architecture: MVVM + Repository pattern, with StateFlow and ViewModel\n- Navigation: Navigation Compose (single-activity)\n- Database: SQLite via SQLiteOpenHelper (no Room, no cloud). Use a DatabaseHelper class with explicit CREATE TABLE statements, CRUD functions, and a DAO-style wrapper. Run all DB calls on Dispatchers.IO via coroutines.\n- Min SDK 26, Target SDK 34\n- Provide build.gradle.kts (app and project), AndroidManifest.xml, and the full package structure\n\n## 3. SPLASH SCREEN (exactly 3 seconds)\n- Show for exactly 3000 ms, then navigate to Home. Remove the splash from the back stack.\n- Dark gradient background (deep navy to purple).\n- Centered animated logo: a crown icon (Leader) that scales in with a spring animation, plus a whistle/megaphone icon (Boss) that fades out and slides away. Draw both with Compose Canvas or Material icons.\n- App name \"BossVsLeader\" fades in letter by letter, with a tagline: \"Lead. Don\'t just boss.\"\n- A thin animated progress bar fills over the full 3 seconds.\n- Implement with LaunchedEffect(Unit) { delay(3000); navigate }.\n\n## 4. ANIMATED TOP NAVIGATION BAR (signature feature)\nBuild a custom animated top bar, not the default TopAppBar:\n- Collapsing behavior: expands to a large header with title and subtitle at the top of the list and shrinks smoothly on scroll (use nestedScroll with TopAppBarDefaults.exitUntilCollapsedScrollBehavior or a custom implementation).\n- Animated gradient background that slowly shifts colors (Boss red/orange to Leader blue/teal) using rememberInfiniteTransition.\n- Animated tab indicator: a pill that slides between tabs (Home, Lessons, Compare, Quiz, Profile) with animateDpAsState and a spring spec. The active tab icon scales and the label fades in.\n- Title cross-fades (AnimatedContent) when the destination changes.\n- Show the user\'s streak as a small flame badge with a pulse animation.\n- Handle edge-to-edge and status bar insets correctly.\n\n## 5. SCREENS\n1. Home: greeting, \"Lesson of the Day\" card, progress ring (Canvas), streak counter, quick-action chips.\n2. Lessons: LazyColumn of lesson cards grouped by category (Communication, Trust, Accountability, Motivation, Decision-Making, Feedback). Each has an icon, title, read time, and a completed checkmark. Tap to open the detail screen.\n3. Lesson Detail: a \"Boss\" panel (red) and a \"Leader\" panel (blue) side by side, with an example scenario, a key takeaway, a bookmark button, and a \"Mark as completed\" button with a confetti or check animation.\n4. Compare: swipeable cards (HorizontalPager) of \"Boss says / Leader says\" pairs, with a flip animation on tap.\n5. Quiz: multiple choice, a progress indicator, animated correct/incorrect feedback, and a final score screen with a retry option. Save the score to SQLite.\n6. Profile: stats (lessons completed, quizzes taken, average score, streak), a bookmarks list, a dark/light theme toggle, and a \"Reset progress\" button with a confirmation dialog.\n\n## 6. SQLITE SCHEMA\n- lessons(id INTEGER PK, title TEXT, category TEXT, boss_text TEXT, leader_text TEXT, scenario TEXT, takeaway TEXT, read_minutes INTEGER, is_completed INTEGER DEFAULT 0, is_bookmarked INTEGER DEFAULT 0)\n- quiz_questions(id INTEGER PK, question TEXT, option_a TEXT, option_b TEXT, option_c TEXT, option_d TEXT, correct_option INTEGER, explanation TEXT, category TEXT)\n- quiz_results(id INTEGER PK, score INTEGER, total INTEGER, taken_at INTEGER)\n- user_stats(id INTEGER PK, streak_days INTEGER, last_active_date TEXT, theme_mode TEXT)\nSeed the database on first launch (onCreate) with at least 20 lessons and 30 quiz questions of real, high-quality content about boss vs leader behavior. Provide the full seed data in code.\n\n## 7. DESIGN\n- Material 3 with a custom ColorScheme: Boss = warm red/orange, Leader = deep blue/teal, neutral surfaces.\n- Full light and dark themes, with dynamic color on Android 12+ as an option.\n- Modern look: rounded 24dp corners, soft elevation, glassmorphism-style cards, gradient accents, generous spacing, and a custom Typography scale.\n- Micro-interactions: animated list item entrance (staggered fade and slide-up), press-scale on cards, and smooth screen transitions (AnimatedNavHost with fade and slide).\n- Use Material Symbols icons (androidx.compose.material:material-icons-extended).\n\n## 8. QUALITY REQUIREMENTS\n- Handle configuration changes and process death (rememberSaveable and ViewModel).\n- Add content descriptions for accessibility and support large font sizes.\n- No crashes on empty states. Show friendly empty-state UIs.\n- Clean code with comments and meaningful names.\n- Output the complete project file tree first, then every file\'s full code in order, then short run instructions for Android Studio.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    }
  }
}
