  planner_response {
    response: "I have successfully built the **BossVsLeader** Android application with Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, and Material 3.\n\n### Summary of Completed Work\n1. **Metadata & Branding**: Configured app name (\"BossVsLeader\"), package namespace, and unique application ID (`com.aistudio.bossvsleader.kxmpzq`).\n2. **SQLite Database & Repository**: Created a robust `DatabaseHelper` (SQLiteOpenHelper) managing `lessons`, `quiz_questions`, `quiz_results`, and `user_stats` tables, pre-seeded with 20 leadership lessons and 30 quiz questions. Integrated asynchronous data operations via `BossLeaderRepository` on `Dispatchers.IO`.\n3. **MVVM & State Management**: Built `MainViewModel` exposing observable `StateFlow` streams for lessons, bookmarks, quiz state, user stats, and category filters.\n4. **Material 3 Theme**: Implemented light and dark color schemes featuring Boss Red (`#D32F2F`) and Leader Blue (`#0288D1`) dynamic accents.\n5. **Splash Screen**: 3-second branded launch screen with spring-animated crown and megaphone icons, tagline, and animated progress bar.\n6. **Animated Top Navigation Bar**: Custom collapsible top bar with a shifting gradient background, streak flame badge with pulse animation, and an interactive tab indicator for Home, Lessons, Compare, Quiz, and Profile.\n7. **Screens**:\n   - **Home**: Daily greeting, progress ring canvas, streak counter, lesson of the day card, and quick-action chips.\n   - **Lessons**: Categorized lazy column with category filters, read times, and completion checkboxes.\n   - **Lesson Detail**: Side-by-side Boss vs Leader behavioral breakdown panels, real-world scenarios, key takeaways, bookmarking, and completion toggles.\n   - **Compare**: Swipeable horizontal pager of interactive \"Boss says vs Leader says\" flip cards.\n   - **Quiz**: Self-paced questions with instant feedback, explanations, score tallying, and persistent score saving to SQLite.\n   - **Profile**: Leadership analytics, bookmarked lessons list, theme toggle (System/Light/Dark), and progress reset confirmation dialog.\n8. **Verification**: Successfully compiled and verified the entire project structure."
    thinking: "**Reviewing Project Build**\n\nI\'m pleased to report a successful build! I\'ve reviewed the output for BossVsLeader. The `metadata.json` file now reflects the updated app name and description, while maintaining core capabilities. Additionally, the root project name has been updated in `settings.gradle.kts`.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have successfully built the **BossVsLeader** Android application with Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, and Material 3.\n\n### Summary of Completed Work\n1. **Metadata & Branding**: Configured app name (\"BossVsLeader\"), package namespace, and unique application ID (`com.aistudio.bossvsleader.kxmpzq`).\n2. **SQLite Database & Repository**: Created a robust `DatabaseHelper` (SQLiteOpenHelper) managing `lessons`, `quiz_questions`, `quiz_results`, and `user_stats` tables, pre-seeded with 20 leadership lessons and 30 quiz questions. Integrated asynchronous data operations via `BossLeaderRepository` on `Dispatchers.IO`.\n3. **MVVM & State Management**: Built `MainViewModel` exposing observable `StateFlow` streams for lessons, bookmarks, quiz state, user stats, and category filters.\n4. **Material 3 Theme**: Implemented light and dark color schemes featuring Boss Red (`#D32F2F`) and Leader Blue (`#0288D1`) dynamic accents.\n5. **Splash Screen**: 3-second branded launch screen with spring-animated crown and megaphone icons, tagline, and animated progress bar.\n6. **Animated Top Navigation Bar**: Custom collapsible top bar with a shifting gradient background, streak flame badge with pulse animation, and an interactive tab indicator for Home, Lessons, Compare, Quiz, and Profile.\n7. **Screens**:\n   - **Home**: Daily greeting, progress ring canvas, streak counter, lesson of the day card, and quick-action chips.\n   - **Lessons**: Categorized lazy column with category filters, read times, and completion checkboxes.\n   - **Lesson Detail**: Side-by-side Boss vs Leader behavioral breakdown panels, real-world scenarios, key takeaways, bookmarking, and completion toggles.\n   - **Compare**: Swipeable horizontal pager of interactive \"Boss says vs Leader says\" flip cards.\n   - **Quiz**: Self-paced questions with instant feedback, explanations, score tallying, and persistent score saving to SQLite.\n   - **Profile**: Leadership analytics, bookmarked lessons list, theme toggle (System/Light/Dark), and progress reset confirmation dialog.\n8. **Verification**: Successfully compiled and verified the entire project structure."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 571108189
